   "claims": [
    "At 120 volts, 0.008333 amps of current are drawn to generate 1 watt of power, and 0.8333 amps are drawn to generate 100 watts.",
    "At 240 volts, 0.004167 amps of current are drawn to generate 1 watt of power, and 0.4167 amps are drawn to generate 100 watts.",
    "For example, let’s calculate how much current in amps a 1,500-watt microwave operating at 120 volts will draw.",
    "I(A) = 1,500 W ÷ 120 V I(A) = 12.5 A So, a 1,500-watt microwave will draw 12.5 amps of current at 120 volts.",
    "Because 1 kilowatt is equal to 1,000 watts, it is also possible to use the formulas above to convert kW to amps, but watts need to be converted to kW first.",
    "Table: Watts to Amps at 120V & 240V AC Table showing watts converted to amps at 120 and 240 volts AC."
   ],
